### 🔎 Search Terms

export star, export *, barrel file, re-export performance, getExportsOfModule, extendExportSymbols, slow check

### 🕗 Version & Regression Information

- Observed on `main` (7.1.0-dev, aa8149273b, 2026-10-09). I have not bisected; the per-name tracking described below has been part of the export resolution code for a long time.

### ⏯ Playground Link

Not reproducible in the playground; it needs a generated project. Generator below.

### 💻 Code

`node gen.mjs && tsgo -p . --extendedDiagnostics`

```js
// One module with many exports, re-exported through a chain of `export *` barrels and imported by many files.
import fs from "node:fs";
const EXPORTS = 20000, DEPTH = 6, USERS = 200;
fs.mkdirSync("src", { recursive: true });
let big = "";
for (let i = 0; i < EXPORTS; i++) big += `export interface Model${i} { id: "${i}"; value: number }\nexport declare function get${i}(): Model${i};\n`;
fs.writeFileSync("src/models.ts", big);
for (let d = 0; d < DEPTH; d++) fs.writeFileSync(`src/barrel${d}.ts`, `export * from "${d === 0 ? "./models" : `./barrel${d - 1}`}";\nexport const barrel${d} = ${d};\n`);
for (let u = 0; u < USERS; u++) fs.writeFileSync(`src/user${u}.ts`, `import { get${u * 7 % EXPORTS} } from "./barrel${DEPTH - 1}";\nexport const v${u} = get${u * 7 % EXPORTS}();\n`);
fs.writeFileSync("tsconfig.json", JSON.stringify({ compilerOptions: { target: "es2022", module: "esnext", moduleResolution: "bundler", strict: true, noEmit: true, types: [], lib: ["es2022"] }, include: ["src"] }));
```

### 🙁 Actual behavior

On an M3 Pro, the 207-file program above takes 0.23 s to check and makes 1.58M allocations. Nearly all of it is resolving the exports of the barrels.

For each module with `export *` declarations, `getExportsOfModuleWorker`:

- clones the module's own export table, and every nested module's table as it visits it;
- merges each re-exported table into a scratch table, allocating an `ExportCollision` struct (with the module specifier text) for every name, to be able to report TS2308 later;
- iterates that per-name table again looking for collisions, then merges the scratch table into the result;
- copies every visited module's export names into a set that is only consulted when an `export type *` was seen.

So each `export *` layer costs several allocations per re-exported name, even with a single `export *`, where nothing can collide.

In a private monorepo (programs of 8.6k and 9.6k files) whose barrels re-export large generated modules, the trackers alone were 5% of all allocations, and `extendExportSymbols` was the top source of map growth in the CPU profile.

### 🙂 Expected behavior

Resolving a module's exports should cost about one map insert per name. Collision bookkeeping should only be needed when a module has more than one `export *`.

### Additional information about the issue

With the change in the linked PR, the generated program checks in 0.05 s with 0.24M allocations, and the monorepo programs check 3.6% and 4.7% faster. Diagnostics and symbol tables are unchanged.

The profiling and the patch were done with Claude Code.

