### 🔎 Search Terms

removePrograms, createPrograms, synthetic program, snapshot update, HandleAPIRequest, nil pointer dereference, SyncMapEntry, typescript/sync, API crash, panic

### 🕗 Version & Regression Information

- This is the behavior in every version I tried: `7.1.0-beta` and `7.1.0-dev.20261021.1` (`typescript@next`)
- I was unable to test this on prior versions because the `createPrograms` / `removePrograms` snapshot API is new in 7.1

This was found working on the migration of ts-loader to TypeScript 7.1: https://github.com/TypeStrong/ts-loader/pull/1704/changes/d159d32047040e606cd1bf6acb5ed6ebedbea107

### ⏯ Playground Link

_N/A - this is the `typescript/sync` API, not the language/checker, so it can't be shown in the Playground. A self-contained repro script is below._

### 💻 Code

```js
// repro.mjs - run with: node repro.mjs (typescript@beta or typescript@next installed)
import fs from "node:fs";
import os from "node:os";
import path from "node:path";
import { API } from "typescript/sync";

const dir = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), "remove-programs-"));
const a = path.join(dir, "a.ts");
const b = path.join(dir, "b.ts");
fs.writeFileSync(a, "export const a = 1;\n");
fs.writeFileSync(b, "export const b = 2;\n");

const api = new API();
const snapshot = api.createSnapshot({
  createPrograms: [{ rootFiles: [a], compilerOptions: {} }],
});
const first = snapshot.operation.createdPrograms[0].id;

// Remove the first synthetic program and create another in the same update.
const next = snapshot.update({
  removePrograms: [first],
  createPrograms: [{ rootFiles: [b], compilerOptions: {} }],
});

console.log(next.operation.createdPrograms[0].getSemanticDiagnostics(b).length);
```

### 🙁 Actual behavior

The `tsgo` server process panics, and the client then fails with `Error: Unexpected EOF while reading from child process (unknown reason)`. Every later request on the same `API` instance fails too (in a webpack build these surface as `EPIPE: broken pipe` / `EBADF: bad file descriptor`).

```
panic: runtime error: invalid memory address or nil pointer dereference [recovered, repanicked]
[signal SIGSEGV: segmentation violation code=0x2 addr=0x0 pc=0x100f97a74]

goroutine 196 [running]:
sync.(*WaitGroup).Go.func1.1()
	sync/waitgroup.go:251 +0x48
panic({0x101d28ba0?, 0x101e7a190?})
	runtime/panic.go:859 +0x120
github.com/microsoft/TypeScript/tsc/internal/project/dirty.(*SyncMapEntry[...]).Value(0x43cf245acd08?)
	github.com/microsoft/TypeScript/tsc/internal/project/dirty/syncmap.go:58 +0x24
github.com/microsoft/TypeScript/tsc/internal/project.(*ProjectCollectionBuilder).HandleAPIRequest.func2()
	github.com/microsoft/TypeScript/tsc/internal/project/projectcollectionbuilder.go:347 +0x4c
sync.(*WaitGroup).Go.func1()
	sync/waitgroup.go:258 +0x48
created by sync.(*WaitGroup).Go in goroutine 1
```

(Trace from `7.1.0-dev.20261021.1`; `7.1.0-beta` panics at the same frames.)

### 🙂 Expected behavior

The update succeeds: the first synthetic program is removed and the second is created, and the script prints `0`.

Making the same two changes as separate updates works on both versions, which is the behavior I'd expect from the combined request too:

```js
const removed = snapshot.update({ removePrograms: [first] });
snapshot.dispose();
const next = removed.update({
  createPrograms: [{ rootFiles: [b], compilerOptions: {} }],
});
// prints 0
```

### Additional information about the issue

- Environment: macOS (Darwin arm64), Node.js v24.18.0.
- Found while integrating the 7.1 API into ts-loader (https://github.com/TypeStrong/ts-loader/pull/1704), which keeps a bounded set of synthetic programs and evicts the oldest when adding a new one - so any project that needed more than the cap of synthetic programs crashed the compiler. ts-loader now sends the removal as its own update as a workaround.
- No `tsconfig.json`, configured project or `openFiles` is needed to reproduce: two synthetic programs are enough.

